WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:04.762
Election Day was coming up everywhere—even at my school.

2
00:00:04.762 --> 00:00:08.722
But I had a problem.

3
00:00:08.723 --> 00:00:12.654
My two best friends were running for school president!

4
00:00:12.654 --> 00:00:17.343
I could only vote for one of them.

5
00:00:17.343 --> 00:00:19.191
Abby is really smart.

6
00:00:19.191 --> 00:00:21.368
She's my next-door neighbor.

7
00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:25.700
She moved here a couple years ago.

8
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.353
Matt is really popular.

9
00:00:28.353 --> 00:00:31.039
I've known him since kindergarten.

10
00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:35.436
We play on the same baseball team.

11
00:00:35.436 --> 00:00:39.670
I helped them make campaign posters to hang in the school hallways.

12
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:43.645
Matt and Abby both said, "Vote for me!"

13
00:00:43.645 --> 00:00:46.746
But how could I choose between my best friends?

14
00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:50.982
Ugh! I wished there was no election.

15
00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:52.669
"Why do we have to vote?"

16
00:00:52.669 --> 00:00:55.934
I asked Mrs. Hardy during social studies.

17
00:00:55.935 --> 00:01:01.434
"Voting is a way for people to show their opinions," she explained.

18
00:01:01.435 --> 00:01:04.935
"Then decisions can be made based on the majority."

19
00:01:04.935 --> 00:01:09.020
That didn't solve my problem.

20
00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.332
I decided to ask my sister about voting.

21
00:01:12.333 --> 00:01:16.203
Becca turned 18 this year.

22
00:01:16.203 --> 00:01:20.506
She can vote in a real election for the first time.

23
00:01:20.506 --> 00:01:22.964
"I can't wait to vote," she said.

24
00:01:22.964 --> 00:01:25.325
"Voting is a privilege!"

25
00:01:25.325 --> 00:01:28.305
"Who are you voting for?" I asked.

26
00:01:28.305 --> 00:01:29.814
"I'm not telling you."

27
00:01:29.815 --> 00:01:32.555
She stuck her tongue out at me.

28
00:01:32.555 --> 00:01:34.117
"Voting is private.

29
00:01:34.117 --> 00:01:38.989
That way people can feel free when they vote."

30
00:01:38.989 --> 00:01:44.621
Downstairs, Mom and Dad were stuffing envelopes.

31
00:01:44.621 --> 00:01:47.905
They volunteer for Mayor Morgan's campaign.

32
00:01:47.905 --> 00:01:51.879
Even our front lawn is filled with campaign signs!

33
00:01:51.879 --> 00:01:56.872
Mom and Dad always say that elections are important.

34
00:01:56.872 --> 00:02:00.662
"We pay taxes to the government," said Mom.

35
00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:03.822
"So we should choose good leaders."

36
00:02:03.822 --> 00:02:06.818
"How do you know who to vote for?" I asked.

37
00:02:06.818 --> 00:02:08.866
"Well," said Dad.

38
00:02:08.866 --> 00:02:13.724
"You have to think hard and know the facts."

39
00:02:13.724 --> 00:02:17.924
"Voting isn't just marking a ballot," added Mom.

40
00:02:17.924 --> 00:02:20.232
"It's a serious responsibility.

41
00:02:20.232 --> 00:02:24.305
I vote for people who will make the world better for us."

42
00:02:24.305 --> 00:02:27.543
My parents didn't solve my problem.

43
00:02:27.543 --> 00:02:30.408
But they had good advice.

44
00:02:30.408 --> 00:02:36.441
I thought really hard about who to vote for.

45
00:02:36.441 --> 00:02:39.569
Abby wanted new classroom computers.

46
00:02:39.569 --> 00:02:42.765
Matt wanted to fix the baseball field.

47
00:02:42.765 --> 00:02:45.674
They both had good ideas.

48
00:02:45.674 --> 00:02:51.255
It wasn't easy, but finally I made a decision.

49
00:02:51.255 --> 00:02:55.079
This morning at school, we voted.

50
00:02:55.079 --> 00:02:58.734
But I'm not saying who I voted for.

51
00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:01.976
Like Becca said, voting is private.

52
00:03:01.977 --> 00:03:04.955
The principal will announce the winner tomorrow.

53
00:03:04.955 --> 00:03:09.816
I know that he—or she!—will be a great school president.

54
00:03:09.816 --> 00:03:16.281
I'm glad I answered my election question.

55
00:03:16.281 --> 00:03:20.815
But now I have a new problem!

56
00:03:20.815 --> 00:03:29.937
How will I cheer up the friend who doesn't win? Oh no!

